          "type": "text",
          "text": "The exterior angles of two regular polygons are in the ratio 2:3. The polygon with the smaller exterior angle has five more sides than the other polygon. Find the larger number of sides."
        }
      ],
      "marks": 3,
      "primary_outcome": "1.6",
      "secondary_outcomes": [],
      "response": {
        "type": "numeric",
